 vishnuroxx/feature-Person-Contact","messageBody":"Feature person contact","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}}]},{"date":"2026-10-12T00:00:00","commitResults":[{"hash":"65b83763b211fc88b1fae53a764f1aa5151718e5","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Make phone and email optional in Person","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":36,"deletions":31},"test-code":{"insertions":63,"deletions":20}}},{"hash":"d34c49c4a850445ed535b60cd6632011202f98bf","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge pull request #72 from vishnuroxx/feature-Person-Contact","messageBody":"Make phone and email Optional in Person","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}},{"hash":"188dbb475c053eb25b2a82dbd2a40e1d1d4b62fe","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Replace address and tags in Person with contexts","messageBody":"Person now has a name, optional phone, optional email and a required,\nnon-empty set of contexts. Address and tags are removed from Person.\n\n- Person: phone and email are Optional; at least one context is required;\n  isSamePerson treats two persons as the same when they share a phone or\n  an email, and ignores the name.\n- Add and edit commands and their parsers use c/ for contexts; add only\n  requires a name and at least one context. An empty c/ on edit is rejected.\n- Storage: JsonAdaptedPerson saves and loads contexts and allows a missing\n  phone or email. Add JsonAdaptedContext.\n- UI, messages and sample data show contexts instead of address and tags.\n- Update tests, test helpers and JSON test data to match.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":170,"deletions":170},"test-code":{"insertions":180,"deletions":344}}},{"hash":"650a6a40abc6cdc1a1a54e29ffbc14d373cba0b2","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Add ParserUtil context tests and use \"person\" in the context message","messageBody":"Add tests for ParserUtil.parseContext and parseContexts, and change\nPerson.MESSAGE_CONTEXT_REQUIRED to say \"person\" instead of \"contact\".\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":1,"deletions":1},"test-code":{"insertions":55,"deletions":0}}}]},{"date":"2026-10-13T00:00:00","commitResults":[{"hash":"e72d6fe47cdccd09f6cb0a9f829475d264e226d2","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Sort contexts on the contact card case-insensitively with String.CASE_INSENSITIVE_ORDER","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":1,"deletions":1}}},{"hash":"3a9fe731732ee97d3adda726d8a0499d9548ca82","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge branch \u0027master\u0027 into feature-Person-Contact","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}},{"hash":"05a59bdc3bf3b0892f5ab2c8ee37608261932e8a","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Update INVALID_PHONE constant for JsonAdaptedPersonTest","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"test-code":{"insertions":1,"deletions":1}}},{"hash":"87aab08de98015cfe8e9a149cda749ce118d3ea0","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge pull request #74 from vishnuroxx/feature-Person-Contact","messageBody":"Replace address and tags in Person with contexts","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}}]},{"date":"2026-10-14T00:00:00","commitResults":[{"hash":"11c4b7af0a7c31b93f53af1b8e509aa6d3fd098f","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Reject null contexts in Person and test the saved form of a context","messageBody":"The Person constructor now throws NullPointerException if the contexts set\ncontains a null element, instead of failing later (for example in\nMessages.format). Add JsonAdaptedContextTest, which also checks that a context\nis saved as a plain string and that the object form is rejected.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":2,"deletions":0},"test-code":{"insertions":72,"deletions":0}}},{"hash":"3f8e5ee97e074e2cc085294796a887a1fab6ac89","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Make saving safer and keep a backup of an unreadable data file","messageBody":"FileUtil.writeToFile now writes to a temporary file and moves it over the\ntarget, so an interrupted save no longer leaves a half-written data file.\n\nWhen the address book data file cannot be loaded, MainApp copies it to\n\u003cname\u003e.bak before starting with an empty address book, so the next save does\nnot overwrite the original. Add FileUtil.backUp and tests for both changes.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":46,"deletions":1},"test-code":{"insertions":93,"deletions":0}}}]},{"date":"2026-10-15T00:00:00","commitResults":[{"hash":"fbd3d98130f91fd450f74a2513d38b4577b119a1","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Remove the unused logger from PersonListPanel","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":0,"deletions":4}}},{"hash":"02a15a960e3984ae7b84fbe2b2dd002d0a516d07","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Recover from null entries in the data file and rename an unreadable file to a timestamped backup","messageBody":"A data file with a null inside it (a null person, a null context, or a file\nthat only contains null) used to escape as a NullPointerException, which was\nnot caught by the DataLoadingException recovery in MainApp, so the app\ncrashed at startup. These cases now throw IllegalValueException or\nDataLoadingException and take the normal recovery path.\n\nFileUtil.backUp now renames the unreadable data file to\n\u003cname\u003e.\u003cUTC time\u003e.bak instead of copying it to \u003cname\u003e.bak. The original name is\nfree for the next save, and an earlier backup keeps its own name. backUp takes\nan optional Clock so tests can fix the time.\n\nAdd regression tests and fixture files for the null cases, and update the\nbackup tests.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":38,"deletions":7},"test-code":{"insertions":86,"deletions":9}}},{"hash":"15e3c3f0d55ea45b770b302a0e62001e04560f16","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge upstream master into feature-Person-Contact","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}},{"hash":"2996845020d1942e0edb1a15334cc5bff32cb07e","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Update the User Guide for the new saving behaviour","messageBody":"Describe how a save is written, what a saved person looks like in the data\nfile, and what happens when the data file cannot be read: it is renamed to\naddressbook.json.\u003cUTC time\u003e.bak and the app starts empty. Add steps to\nrecover the data and an FAQ entry for an unexpectedly empty list.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"docs":{"insertions":43,"deletions":2}}},{"hash":"cd538ebbca5f34c346787a727f097cdc700319e7","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge pull request #95 from vishnuroxx/feature-Person-Contact","messageBody":"Make saving safer and keep a backup of an unreadable data file","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}}]}],"ryan24chua":[{"date":"2026-10-01T00:00:00","commitResults":[{"hash":"db8713cdeb542ea192e8c762f61b9a2bc0aa52fa","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Update Ryan\u0027s details in AboutUs.md","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"docs":{"insertions":3,"deletions":4}}},{"hash":"e06dae670dc9d423c2236e075bd92cba4603e297","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge pull request #14 from vishnuroxx/T-UpdateAboutUs","messageBody":"Update AboutUs.md to include details about Vishnu","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}},{"hash":"814937ad38adf5fdd750882afeeb74157e42f8a5","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge pull request #17 from Totonyny511/7-update-about-us","messageBody":"Update Tony\u0027s details in AboutUs.md","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}},{"hash":"faaffbfb7c3853da36b384aafb9dec34ebbbae04","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge pull request #21 from ryan24chua/20-update-ryans-details","messageBody":"Update Ryan\u0027s details in AboutUs.md","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}},{"hash":"3d193b623ef85e1594ec128fa39f8a97eb7c1899","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge branch \u0027master\u0027 into update-about-us-chen-sixian","messageBody":"